  "verbalization": "Bleomycin is linked to Leukocyte common antigen through a series of molecular interactions involving 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which acts as a target of multiple entities, including bleomycin and Lysine-specific demethylase 4C. This suggests that bleomycin may exert its effects through a common intermediary, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets the Leukocyte common antigen. The presence of multiple pathways converging on this compound indicates a potential mechanism where bleomycin could influence leukocyte function via this shared target. The evidence supports a role for 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a bridge between bleomycin and the Leukocyte common antigen, highlighting a possible regulatory or signaling pathway that is modulated by bleomycin.",
